    "title": "Rapper King Harris, son of T.I., arrested in Gwinnett County for speeding, obstruction",
    "text": "King Harris, a 21-year-old Atlanta-based rapper and the son of legendary Atlanta rapper T.I., was arrested on Sunday in Gwinnett County.According to the Gwinnett County Police Department (GCPD), Harris was traveling at around 80 mph in a 45-mph zone in a Tesla Cybertruck near Holcomb Bridge Road and Peachtree Corners Circle in Peachtree Corners.GCPD also says Harris was \"drifting within and outside of his lane and failing to use turn signals.\"The police department posted the bodycam footage, which is also embedded below. In the footage, Harris can be seen telling officers he did not know he was traveling that fast.After a handgun was observed in plain view, Harris was asked to step out of the vehicle but initially refused. Harris told the officer he did not feel safe and called his attorney.The attorney told him he needed to get out of the vehicle.\"So this make y'all feel tough?\" Harris could be heard askingthe officers.T.I. showed up to speak with the officers.\"Did he express his fear for safety?\" T.I. asked the officers. The officers explained that Harris had to get out of the vehicle upon arrest.Harris was taken into custody without further incident, and was allegedly found with an oxycodone pill on his person leading to additional charges.He was charged with obstruction, possession of a schedule II controlled substance, speeding, and a seatbelt violation.",
